而且我姐姐丈夫的名字叫德怀特。

622
00:26:47.640 --> 00:26:48.560
Isn't that crazy?
这不是很巧吗？

623
00:26:48.560 --> 00:26:50.460
Now, the writers didn't know that.
编剧们当时并不知道这一点。

624
00:26:50.540 --> 00:26:52.300
That was just all, like, by chance.
这一切纯属巧合。

625
00:26:52.560 --> 00:26:52.840
Yes.
是的。

626
00:26:53.020 --> 00:26:54.380
Here's a little bit of interesting trivia.
这里有个有趣的小花絮。

627
00:26:54.380 --> 00:27:01.060
Yeah, my father's name is Jim, my brother-in-law's name is Dwight, and my niece's name is Cece.
是啊，我父亲叫吉姆，我姐夫叫德怀特，我侄女叫西西。

628
00:27:01.760 --> 00:27:04.640
Well, and they named the character after Cece.
而且他们是以西西的名字来命名那个角色的。

629
00:27:04.800 --> 00:27:04.960
Yes.
是的。

630
00:27:05.060 --> 00:27:07.140
The other two were already happening.
另外两个名字纯属巧合。

631
00:27:07.340 --> 00:27:07.520
Yeah.
是啊。

632
00:27:07.720 --> 00:27:09.260
But that one was all you.
但那个名字完全是你提议的。

633
00:27:09.400 --> 00:27:15.380
My niece, Cece, was born about a week before we filmed the episode where Pam and Jim have
我侄女西西是在我们拍摄帕姆和吉姆生孩子那一集的前一周出生的，

634
00:27:15.380 --> 00:27:19.240
their baby, and I asked if we could name their baby Cece after my niece.
我问能不能用我侄女的名字西西来给他们的孩子命名。

635
00:27:19.340 --> 00:27:20.260
I think that's so cute.
我觉得这太可爱了。

636
00:27:20.540 --> 00:27:21.800
All right, ladies, should we take a break?
好了，女士们，我们要休息一下吗？

637
00:27:22.120 --> 00:27:22.840
I think we should.
我觉得应该休息一下。

638
00:27:22.840 --> 00:27:25.160
I see you've pared down your note cards here.
我看到你把笔记卡精简了不少。

639
00:27:25.160 --> 00:27:26.320
I'm paring down my note cards.
我正在精简我的笔记卡。

640
00:27:26.320 --> 00:27:27.360
I've collected myself.
我已经调整好状态了。

641
00:27:27.580 --> 00:27:30.100
I'm no longer laughing at you when you just simply look at me.
你看着我的时候，我不会再嘲笑你了。

642
00:27:30.560 --> 00:27:31.260
Thank you.
谢谢。

643
00:27:31.440 --> 00:27:34.520
Thank you for admitting that all I'm doing is looking at you.
谢谢你承认我只是在看着你。

644
00:27:34.640 --> 00:27:37.160
I know, but the expression was really funny.
我知道，但那个表情真的很好笑。

645
00:27:37.160 --> 00:27:37.360
Why?
为什么？

646
00:27:37.540 --> 00:27:38.880
Now you just did it again.
你现在又那样了。

647
00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:39.180
Okay.
好吧。

648
00:27:39.180 --> 00:27:42.480
You just implied that there's some way I'm looking at you.
你刚才暗示我看着你的方式有什么特别之处。

649
00:27:42.620 --> 00:27:42.880
Ugh.
呃。

650
00:27:43.140 --> 00:27:44.100
This is your thing.
这是你的招牌动作。

651
00:27:44.300 --> 00:27:46.240
I'm going to take a sneaky photo of your face.
我要偷偷拍一张你的脸。

652
00:27:46.500 --> 00:27:47.340
Don't you dare.
你敢。

653
00:27:47.860 --> 00:27:48.580
Lady, you do.
女士，你确实有。

654
00:27:48.660 --> 00:27:49.720
I have to do the impression.
我得模仿一下。

655
00:27:49.980 --> 00:27:50.160
Ready?
准备好了吗？

656
00:27:50.820 --> 00:27:51.800
This is my impression.
这就是我的模仿。

657
00:27:51.980 --> 00:27:52.540
You be me.
你来演我。

658
00:27:52.540 --> 00:27:53.120
Hold on.
等一下。

659
00:27:53.240 --> 00:27:55.460
Look down at your note, whatever you're doing.
低头看你的笔记，不管你在做什么。

660
00:27:55.680 --> 00:27:56.100
Okay.
好的。

661
00:27:56.460 --> 00:27:56.680
Ready?
准备好了吗？

662
00:27:56.980 --> 00:27:57.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

663
00:27:58.480 --> 00:28:00.360
And those are my fast facts.
以上就是我的快讯。

664
00:28:00.960 --> 00:28:01.520
Nothing?
什么都没有？

665
00:28:01.820 --> 00:28:02.660
You have nothing?
你什么都没说？

666
00:28:03.980 --> 00:28:05.900
Angela, this is a podcaSt.
安吉拉，这是播客。

667
00:28:05.900 --> 00:28:07.020
You're supposed to talk.
你应该说话的。

668
00:28:07.220 --> 00:28:08.080
That's my impression.
那就是我的模仿。

669
00:28:08.800 --> 00:28:10.500
But did you see my face?
但你看到我的表情了吗？

670
00:28:11.200 --> 00:28:11.760
Barely.
勉强看到了。

671
00:28:12.120 --> 00:28:13.440
Those are my fast facts.
以上就是我的快讯。

672
00:28:13.680 --> 00:28:13.760
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

673
00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:15.280
And those are my fast facts.
以上就是我的快讯。

674
00:28:15.500 --> 00:28:16.160
Your turn.
轮到你了。

675
00:28:22.360 --> 00:28:22.800
Okay.
好的。

676
00:28:22.800 --> 00:28:23.900
We are back.
我们回来了。

677
00:28:24.460 --> 00:28:28.180
Michael and Jan are getting ready to leave to go to Chili's for their big meeting.
迈克尔和简正准备出发去Chili's参加他们的大会议。

678
00:28:28.360 --> 00:28:32.900
And did you notice in the parking lot, Michael says Chili's is just a couple blocks away.
你有没有注意到在停车场里，迈克尔说Chili's就在几个街区外。

679
00:28:33.160 --> 00:28:34.280
They should just drive together.
他们本该一起开车去的。

680
00:28:35.800 --> 00:28:44.860
However, the closest Chili's is actually about 30 minutes away in Wilkes-Barre at the Wyoming Valley Mall.
然而，最近的Chili's其实在约30分钟路程外的威尔克斯-巴里，位于怀俄明谷购物中心。

681
00:28:45.040 --> 00:28:47.460
Somebody did a little bit of a deep dive.
有人做了一番深入调查。

682
00:28:47.460 --> 00:28:48.700
I remember this.
我记得这个。

683
00:28:48.920 --> 00:28:55.920
I remember when we were shooting it that we discovered that there isn't really a Chili's in Scranton.
我记得拍摄的时候我们发现斯克兰顿其实并没有Chili's。

684
00:28:56.360 --> 00:28:57.780
You have to go outside.
你得去外地。

685
00:28:58.080 --> 00:28:58.440
Oh.
哦。

686
00:28:58.640 --> 00:28:59.280
To get there.
才能去那里。

687
00:28:59.960 --> 00:29:02.340
And it wasn't a big deal when we did the Dundies.
我们拍邓迪奖的时候这倒不是什么大问题。

688
00:29:02.680 --> 00:29:05.800
But here, Michael does say it's only a couple blocks away.
但在这里，迈克尔确实说它只有几个街区远。

689
00:29:05.960 --> 00:29:06.380
But it's not.
但事实并非如此。

690
00:29:06.540 --> 00:29:09.380
And then he goes on to say, you don't know Scranton at all.
然后他接着说，你根本不了解斯克兰顿。

691
00:29:10.260 --> 00:29:10.900
That's right.
没错。

692
00:29:10.900 --> 00:29:14.000
It's like, well, maybe, maybe you don't know it.
就像是，好吧，也许，也许是你自己不了解。

693
00:29:14.160 --> 00:29:17.920
What was it like for all the people in Scranton to see this episode and be like, wait, what?
斯克兰顿的人们看到这一集时是什么反应，会不会觉得，等等，什么？

694
00:29:18.080 --> 00:29:18.880
Where's the Chili's?
Chili's在哪里？

695
00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:22.420
Well, they probably had the same moment when they saw a palm tree or two every once in a while.
嗯，他们看到偶尔出现的一两棵棕榈树时，可能也有过同样的反应。

696
00:29:22.520 --> 00:29:24.500
They'd be like, wait, what's a palm tree doing in there?
他们会想，等等，那里面怎么会有棕榈树？

697
00:29:24.640 --> 00:29:26.420
I also want to say, I looked it up.
我还想说，我查过了。

698
00:29:26.540 --> 00:29:28.260
There still isn't a Chili's in Scranton.
斯克兰顿现在依然没有Chili's。

699
00:29:28.660 --> 00:29:29.020
Chili's?
Chili's？

700
00:29:29.480 --> 00:29:30.560
Missed opportunity here?
错失良机了吗？

701
00:29:30.740 --> 00:29:33.220
You guys want to go ahead and put a Chili's in Scranton already?
你们几个打算什么时候在斯克兰顿开一家Chili's餐厅？

702
00:29:34.020 --> 00:29:37.420
Chili's, maybe you should call us because Jenna has some business plan for you.
Chili's，也许你们该给我们打个电话，因为珍娜有个商业计划要给你们看。

703
00:29:37.480 --> 00:29:38.600
We will cut the ribbon.
我们会去剪彩的。

704
00:29:39.440 --> 00:29:40.780
Oh, we would cut the ribbon.
哦，我们肯定会去剪彩的。

705
00:29:40.900 --> 00:29:41.440
We'll cut the ribbon.
我们会剪彩的。

706
00:29:41.680 --> 00:29:42.180
I've never done that.
我从来没做过那种事。

707
00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:42.800
That'd be fun.
那一定会很有趣。

708
00:29:42.920 --> 00:29:43.240
I know.
我知道。

709
00:29:43.380 --> 00:29:45.520
I've always wanted to do that where you hold the giant scissors.
我一直想试试那种拿着巨大剪刀剪彩的感觉。

710
00:29:46.060 --> 00:29:47.120
Don't chunk them, though.
不过别乱扔剪刀。

711
00:29:47.420 --> 00:29:48.740
I won't chunk them, Angela.
我不会乱扔的，安吉拉。

712
00:29:48.820 --> 00:29:50.140
I will not chunk them at anyone.
我绝不会拿剪刀对着任何人乱扔。

713
00:29:51.080 --> 00:29:55.740
So they walk inside the Chili's to one of my all-time favorite scenes.
于是他们走进Chili's，来到了我最喜欢的场景之一。

714
00:29:55.880 --> 00:29:56.660
Yes, I bet.
是啊，我敢打赌。

715
00:29:56.660 --> 00:29:57.420
I bet it's this.
我猜就是这一段。

716
00:29:57.560 --> 00:29:58.500
I'm holding up my note card.
我正举着我的笔记卡。

717
00:30:10.900 --> 00:30:12.780
Let's see everything in him go electric.
看看他全身触电般的感觉。

718
00:30:12.940 --> 00:30:13.240
Yes.
没错。

719
00:30:13.360 --> 00:30:14.120
Is Gould dead?
古尔德死了吗？

720
00:30:14.820 --> 00:30:16.220
Do you want to talk about it?
你想谈谈这个吗？

721
00:30:16.440 --> 00:30:17.200
Are you okay?
你还好吗？

722
00:30:17.440 --> 00:30:18.440
We're in a meeting, Michael.
我们在开会呢，迈克尔。

723
00:30:18.680 --> 00:30:19.720
Michael, we're in a meeting.
迈克尔，我们在开会。

724
00:30:19.920 --> 00:30:21.360
And then he has to give that look to camera?
然后他必须对着镜头露出那个表情？

725
00:30:21.580 --> 00:30:21.840
Yeah.
没错。

726
00:30:22.220 --> 00:30:23.100
Oh my God.
天哪。

727
00:30:23.260 --> 00:30:24.160
It's so good.
太棒了。

728
00:30:24.320 --> 00:30:26.180
Oh man, Steve is so good in that scene.
天呐，史蒂夫在那场戏里演得真好。

729
00:30:26.520 --> 00:30:28.800
Oh, we have the same thing written down now.
哦，我们现在写的东西一模一样。

730
00:30:28.880 --> 00:30:29.100
What?
什么？

731
00:30:29.180 --> 00:30:30.740
I just peeked at your note card.
我刚才偷看了你的笔记卡。

732
00:30:30.840 --> 00:30:31.700
The waitress, Megan.
女服务员，梅根。

733
00:30:31.700 --> 00:30:36.400
You hold your paper up so I can't see it, but my note cards are right here in front
你把纸举起来不让我看，但我的笔记卡就放在你面前。

734
00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:36.680
of you.
那是你的事。

735
00:30:36.720 --> 00:30:37.600
That's your business.
那是你的生意。

736
00:30:38.020 --> 00:30:39.720
Five minutes, 47 seconds.
5分47秒。

737
00:30:40.040 --> 00:30:42.380
Megan, may we have an awesome blossom, please?
梅根，能给我们来一份超赞花球吗？

738
00:30:42.740 --> 00:30:43.940
I think this is a great detail.
我觉得这是一个很棒的细节。

739
00:30:44.040 --> 00:30:45.360
Now, I don't know if this was in the script.
现在，我不知道这是否在剧本里。

740
00:30:45.360 --> 00:30:52.180
I don't know if Steve improvised that, but I love that Michael remembers the waitress
我不知道这是不是史蒂夫即兴发挥的，但我很喜欢迈克尔能记住女服务员

741
00:30:52.180 --> 00:30:52.780
by name.
名字这一点。

742
00:30:52.880 --> 00:30:57.720
I absolutely believe that the character of Michael would remember every waiter or waitress
我绝对相信迈克尔这个角色会记住每一位服务员

743
00:30:57.720 --> 00:30:58.200
by name.
的名字。

744
00:30:58.400 --> 00:30:59.420
I think that Michael-
我觉得迈克尔——

745
00:30:59.420 --> 00:31:00.000
Every flight attendant.
还有每一位空乘人员。

746
00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.960
Yes, I was going to say, I think Michael knows the name of every person he has to interact
没错，我正想说，我觉得迈克尔记得他必须打交道的每一个人的名字。

747
00:31:03.960 --> 00:31:04.320
with.
没错。

748
00:31:04.400 --> 00:31:04.620
Yes.
是的。

749
00:31:04.800 --> 00:31:06.920
And it's his pleasure to get to know their name.
而且他很乐意去了解他们的名字。

750
00:31:06.920 --> 00:31:09.600
And I love that he knows the waitress as Megan.
我真的很喜欢他记得那个女服务员叫梅根。

751
00:31:09.840 --> 00:31:11.660
It is a great, great detail.
这是一个非常、非常棒的细节。

752
00:31:12.560 --> 00:31:18.840
Six minutes, 19 seconds, Michael calls Pam on the phone back at the office to get him to
在6分19秒时，迈克尔给办公室里的帕姆打电话，让她

753
00:31:18.840 --> 00:31:23.820
read her a bunch of jokes from these joke books in his office.
读给他听办公室里那些笑话书里的一堆笑话。

754
00:31:23.820 --> 00:31:29.040
I got a lot of questions about this, people wanting to know the punchline for that joke
我收到了很多关于这个的问题，人们想知道那个关于灯塔的笑话的笑点是什么，

755
00:31:29.040 --> 00:31:33.520
about the lighthouse that Pam starts and Michael's like, no, no, no, no, not that one.
帕姆刚开了个头，迈克尔就说，不，不，不，不，不是那个。

756
00:31:33.860 --> 00:31:35.560
There is no punchline to the joke.
那个笑话根本没有笑点。

757
00:31:35.820 --> 00:31:37.140
It was not in the book.
书里根本就没有。

758
00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:43.560
Those jokes, quote unquote, were scripted and they just wrote the beginning of the jokes.
那些所谓的“笑话”是有剧本的，他们只写了笑话的开头。

759
00:31:43.860 --> 00:31:44.560
Oh, I love it.
哦，我喜欢这个。

760
00:31:44.600 --> 00:31:45.320
There were no endings.
根本没有结尾。

761
00:31:45.560 --> 00:31:47.260
I bet the writers had a lot of fun with that.
我敢说编剧们写的时候一定很开心。

762
00:31:47.420 --> 00:31:50.960
Just writing the first line of a joke that they know they don't have to worry about
只写一个笑话的第一句，而且他们知道根本不用担心

763
00:31:50.960 --> 00:31:51.540
the payoff.
后续的包袱。

764
00:31:51.820 --> 00:31:52.600
That would have been fun.
那一定很有趣。

765
00:31:52.600 --> 00:31:57.940
Well, and I had the challenge of having to memorize the line, but look like I was reading
嗯，我当时面临的挑战是既要背下那句台词，又要装作是在读

766
00:31:57.940 --> 00:31:59.720
from the book that I was not reading from.
那本其实我根本没在读的书。

767
00:31:59.900 --> 00:32:00.160
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

768
00:32:00.220 --> 00:32:00.720
That's tricky.
那挺难的。

769
00:32:00.840 --> 00:32:01.520
It was a little tricky.
确实有点难。

770
00:32:01.720 --> 00:32:08.000
After this, Pam finds Threat Level Midnight, the script that Michael has written, where he
在这之后，帕姆发现了《威胁等级：午夜》，那是迈克尔写的剧本，他在里面

771
00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:11.640
is an action star, Michael Skarn.
饰演动作明星迈克尔·斯卡恩。

772
00:32:12.260 --> 00:32:20.140
And at 7 minutes, 18 seconds, Jim finds drawings of the Threat Level Midnight poster in the
在7分18秒时，吉姆在剧本里发现了《威胁等级：午夜》海报的草图。

773
00:32:20.140 --> 00:32:20.420
script.
我们收到了一位粉丝贝卡·拉米雷斯的提问。

774
00:32:20.460 --> 00:32:23.160
And we had a fan question from Becca Ramirez.
她问，剧本里《威胁等级：午夜》的那些画是谁画的？

775
00:32:23.460 --> 00:32:27.500
She asked, who made the drawings in the script of Threat Level Midnight?
你知道吗？

776
00:32:27.600 --> 00:32:27.960
Do you know?
我不知道。

777
00:32:28.120 --> 00:32:28.720
I don't.
好问题。

778
00:32:28.880 --> 00:32:29.580
Great question.
格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

779
00:32:29.900 --> 00:32:30.980
Greg Daniels.
真的吗？

780
00:32:31.100 --> 00:32:31.860
Did he really?
是他自己画的。

781
00:32:31.880 --> 00:32:33.500
He made the drawings himself.
天哪。

782
00:32:33.820 --> 00:32:34.460
Oh, my gosh.
我能想象他坐在旁边快速涂鸦的样子。

783
00:32:34.500 --> 00:32:36.920
I could see him sort of sitting on the side quickly drawing them.
所以他画了草图，然后交给了，我想应该是菲尔·谢伊。

784
00:32:36.920 --> 00:32:42.600
So he sketched them out, and then he gave them to, I guess it would be Phil Shea.
是的。

785
00:32:42.720 --> 00:32:42.940
Yeah.
然后菲尔雇了一位艺术家。

786
00:32:43.360 --> 00:32:44.940
And Phil hired an artiSt.
但这只是个参考。

787
00:32:45.060 --> 00:32:46.580
But this was the example.
格雷格画草图是为了表达，这是我对海报的想法，这就是

