00:45:11.020 --> 00:45:14.600
But as you see in the show, it's an unfinished script.
但正如你在剧中看到的，那是一个未完成的剧本。

1092
00:45:14.600 --> 00:45:16.420
So it was not a fully written script.
所以它并不是一个写完整的剧本。

1093
00:45:16.640 --> 00:45:20.560
They also wanted to know if we read from the script or if it was improvised.
他们还想知道我们是照着剧本读的，还是即兴发挥的。

1094
00:45:21.220 --> 00:45:24.520
I was going to say that I thought we read from the script.
我本来想说我觉得我们是照着剧本读的。

1095
00:45:24.840 --> 00:45:31.200
But I found an interview with Brian Baumgartner where he said we improvised it.
但我发现布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳的一次采访，他说我们是即兴发挥的。

1096
00:45:31.360 --> 00:45:32.820
And BJ backed that up.
而且B.J.也证实了这一点。

1097
00:45:33.040 --> 00:45:37.160
That we were sitting around for about five to ten minutes.
说我们当时坐在那里大约五到十分钟。

1098
00:45:37.500 --> 00:45:41.180
And we were just throwing out anything at all.
我们只是随口胡诌。

1099
00:45:41.300 --> 00:45:43.000
Which seems almost impossible to me.
这对我来说似乎几乎是不可能的。

1100
00:45:43.080 --> 00:45:45.300
But there's two people in the cast who say that's how it was.
但剧组里有两个人说当时就是那样。

1101
00:45:45.380 --> 00:45:46.200
I remember it differently.
我的记忆和这不一样。

1102
00:45:46.200 --> 00:45:49.380
Even Phyllis when she said, I have two things to say.
连菲利斯说那句“我有两件事要说”的时候也是。

1103
00:45:49.500 --> 00:45:50.620
First thing is I love you.
第一件事是我爱你。

1104
00:45:51.420 --> 00:45:52.020
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

1105
00:45:52.120 --> 00:45:54.960
So I should say some of it was scripted.
所以我得说，其中一部分是有剧本的。

1106
00:45:55.120 --> 00:45:57.940
But we did also improvise some.
但我们也确实即兴发挥了一些。

1107
00:45:58.160 --> 00:45:58.400
Okay.
好的。

1108
00:45:58.540 --> 00:45:59.200
So it was both.
所以两者都有。

1109
00:45:59.340 --> 00:46:00.820
And that happened a lot when we were shooting.
我们在拍摄时经常发生这种情况。

1110
00:46:01.000 --> 00:46:02.380
They would leave the cameras rolling.
他们会让摄像机一直开着。

1111
00:46:02.780 --> 00:46:02.960
Yeah.
没错。

1112
00:46:03.020 --> 00:46:05.080
And then we would throw stuff out there.
然后我们会抛出一些即兴的内容。

1113
00:46:05.160 --> 00:46:07.540
And some of the improvisations stayed in.
其中一些即兴发挥被保留了下来。

1114
00:46:07.740 --> 00:46:08.360
I love that.
我喜欢这样。

1115
00:46:08.480 --> 00:46:10.940
But you could definitely tell the beginning of the scene was scripted.
但你绝对能看出来场景的开头是有剧本的。

1116
00:46:11.040 --> 00:46:11.120
Yes.
是的。

1117
00:46:11.120 --> 00:46:12.140
Getting you into it.
为了把你带入情境。

1118
00:46:12.240 --> 00:46:12.920
Yes, that's true.
是的，没错。

1119
00:46:12.920 --> 00:46:17.820
Back at Chili's, guys, let's have a little bit of an adult beverage time code count.
回到Chili's餐厅，伙计们，让我们来统计一下成人饮品的时间码。

1120
00:46:18.000 --> 00:46:18.400
Oh, dear.
噢，天哪。

1121
00:46:18.820 --> 00:46:22.740
So at 7 minutes 59 seconds, Jan orders a vodka tonic.
在7分59秒时，简点了一杯伏特加汤力水。

1122
00:46:22.860 --> 00:46:24.620
We never see this vodka tonic.
我们从没见过这杯伏特加汤力水。

1123
00:46:24.860 --> 00:46:25.840
Oh, that's right.
噢，对哦。

1124
00:46:26.040 --> 00:46:26.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1125
00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:29.480
At 8 minutes 35 seconds, they all have margaritas.
在8分35秒时，他们都喝上了玛格丽特。

1126
00:46:30.060 --> 00:46:32.320
So is Jan on her second drink?
所以简是在喝第二杯吗？

1127
00:46:32.680 --> 00:46:36.080
At 13 minutes 44 seconds, Michael and Christian are having beers.
在13分44秒时，迈克尔和克里斯蒂安在喝啤酒。

1128
00:46:36.480 --> 00:46:38.740
Jan looks like she's having a water with lime.
简看起来像是在喝加青柠的水。

1129
00:46:38.860 --> 00:46:39.400
I can't tell.
我看不出来。

1130
00:46:39.540 --> 00:46:40.600
It's in a tall glass.
装在一个高杯子里。

1131
00:46:40.600 --> 00:46:42.960
Maybe that's finally her vodka tonic.
也许那终于就是她的伏特加汤力水了。

1132
00:46:43.020 --> 00:46:43.680
I don't know.
我不知道。

1133
00:46:43.900 --> 00:46:47.520
That's our adult beverage count for those of you who love the background stuff like me.
这就是我们为那些像我一样喜欢背景细节的观众准备的成人饮品统计。

1134
00:46:47.860 --> 00:46:50.360
Angela, I'm ready to take us on a date.
安吉拉，我准备好带我们去约会了。

1135
00:46:50.560 --> 00:46:51.180
To the roof.
去屋顶。

1136
00:46:51.360 --> 00:46:51.920
To the roof.
去屋顶。

1137
00:46:52.160 --> 00:46:54.020
Pam and Jim's roof date.
帕姆和吉姆的屋顶约会。

1138
00:46:54.340 --> 00:46:55.460
I have so many questions.
我有好多问题。

1139
00:46:55.800 --> 00:46:58.180
I have so many technical questions.
我有好多技术层面的问题。

1140
00:46:58.360 --> 00:46:58.600
Okay.
好的。

1141
00:46:58.660 --> 00:47:02.080
And then I have some just, you know, fan of the office questions.
然后我还有一些，你知道的，作为《办公室》粉丝的问题。

1142
00:47:02.140 --> 00:47:02.740
What do you want to know?
你想知道什么？

1143
00:47:03.000 --> 00:47:04.460
How did you get up on that roof?
你们是怎么上到那个屋顶的？

1144
00:47:04.600 --> 00:47:04.960
Okay.
好的。

1145
00:47:04.980 --> 00:47:10.220
So the ladder that you see in the episode really leads up to the roof.
剧集中你看到的那个梯子确实通往屋顶。

1146
00:47:10.220 --> 00:47:13.080
Do you really climb that little fire escape looking ladder?
你们真的爬了那个看起来像消防通道的小梯子吗？

1147
00:47:13.320 --> 00:47:14.440
John and I did not.
约翰和我没有。

1148
00:47:14.600 --> 00:47:16.380
But that is how the crew got up there.
但那是工作人员上去的方式。

1149
00:47:16.580 --> 00:47:16.780
Okay.
好的。

1150
00:47:17.280 --> 00:47:20.220
John and I, for I guess...
约翰和我，我想是因为……

1151
00:47:20.220 --> 00:47:21.000
Safety reasons?
出于安全考虑？

1152
00:47:21.120 --> 00:47:22.180
And insurance reasons.
还有保险方面的考虑。

1153
00:47:22.460 --> 00:47:24.860
We got into a harness.
我们系上了安全带。

1154
00:47:25.280 --> 00:47:25.680
Okay.
好吧。

1155
00:47:25.680 --> 00:47:29.280
And then they lifted us up to the roof.
然后他们把我们升到了屋顶上。

1156
00:47:29.540 --> 00:47:31.200
Like in a forklift kind of thing?
就像叉车那样的东西吗？

1157
00:47:31.240 --> 00:47:31.540
Yeah.
是的。

1158
00:47:31.800 --> 00:47:38.920
In some sort of weird platformy forklift, which seemed scarier and more dangerous than if I'd
是一种奇怪的平台式叉车，感觉比让我直接用梯子爬上去还要吓人、还要危险。

1159
00:47:38.920 --> 00:47:40.600
just been allowed to use the ladder.
直接让我用梯子就好了。

1160
00:47:40.780 --> 00:47:46.400
And we shot on the actual roof of Dunder Mifflin, of the Dunder Mifflin building.
而且我们是在真正的邓德·米夫林大楼的屋顶上拍摄的。

1161
00:47:46.660 --> 00:47:47.300
I would rather climb the ladder.
我宁愿爬梯子。

1162
00:47:47.580 --> 00:47:48.120
Same.
我也是。

1163
00:47:48.320 --> 00:47:49.920
I asked to climb the ladder.
我当时也要求爬梯子来着。

1164
00:47:49.920 --> 00:47:53.940
But we went up and down on the platform forklift.
但我们还是坐那个平台叉车上上下下的。

1165
00:47:54.200 --> 00:47:54.440
Okay.
好吧。

1166
00:47:56.160 --> 00:47:58.060
I have a fan question about the roof.
我有一个粉丝关于屋顶的问题。

1167
00:47:58.480 --> 00:47:58.940
Okay.
好的。

1168
00:47:59.160 --> 00:47:59.820
James K.
詹姆斯·K。

1169
00:48:00.140 --> 00:48:01.820
asked, was it cold on the roof?
问，屋顶上冷吗？

1170
00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:02.980
It looked cold.
看起来挺冷的。

1171
00:48:03.180 --> 00:48:03.940
It wasn't.
并不冷。

1172
00:48:04.180 --> 00:48:04.980
It wasn't?
不冷吗？

1173
00:48:05.040 --> 00:48:11.120
Oh, Angela, shooting the scene is one of my fondest memories of all time from the show.
噢，安吉拉，拍摄那场戏是我在剧组最美好的回忆之一。

1174
00:48:11.120 --> 00:48:19.360
Because the only people on the roof were me, John, Greg Daniels, Paul Lieberstein, our first
因为屋顶上只有我、约翰、格雷格·丹尼尔斯、保罗·利伯斯坦、我们的第一副导演，

1175
00:48:19.360 --> 00:48:22.820
AD, and our camera operator and DP, Randall Einhorn.
还有我们的摄像师和摄影指导兰德尔·艾因霍恩。

1176
00:48:23.540 --> 00:48:24.840
It was warm.
当时很暖和。

1177
00:48:24.980 --> 00:48:27.140
It was a warm summer evening.
那是一个温暖的夏夜。

1178
00:48:27.360 --> 00:48:28.840
But like a beautiful summer night.
就像一个美丽的夏夜。

1179
00:48:29.180 --> 00:48:30.420
Warm breeze.
有温暖的微风。

1180
00:48:31.700 --> 00:48:39.840
It was, I can't explain it, but this little group of us up on the roof, it hit me while
我没法解释，但我们这群人在屋顶上的时候，我突然意识到，

1181
00:48:39.840 --> 00:48:40.620
I was up there.
我正在拍电视剧。

1182
00:48:41.640 --> 00:48:43.140
I'm on a TV show.
我正在实现我的梦想。

1183
00:48:43.320 --> 00:48:44.700
I'm living my dream.
这太棒了。

1184
00:48:45.660 --> 00:48:47.140
This is amazing.
真的。

1185
00:48:47.400 --> 00:48:47.900
Right.
没错。

1186
00:48:48.080 --> 00:48:49.660
I'm sure it felt really magical.
我敢肯定那感觉一定很神奇。

1187
00:48:50.020 --> 00:48:51.280
Just like a magical moment.
就像一个神奇的时刻。

1188
00:48:51.620 --> 00:48:52.680
Completely magical.
完全是神奇的。

1189
00:48:52.680 --> 00:48:55.420
We had really gelled as a group at this point.
那时我们作为一个团队已经非常有默契了。

1190
00:48:55.680 --> 00:48:57.600
You know, we were really in it all together.
你知道，我们真的齐心协力。

1191
00:48:57.940 --> 00:49:00.240
We all loved the show so much.
我们都非常热爱这部剧。

1192
00:49:00.520 --> 00:49:03.100
We loved being at work so much.
我们非常热爱这份工作。

1193
00:49:03.280 --> 00:49:05.600
It was just really, really special.
那段时光真的非常、非常特别。

1194
00:49:05.920 --> 00:49:09.020
And the grilled cheese sandwiches tasted so good.
而且烤奶酪三明治吃起来太美味了。

1195
00:49:09.840 --> 00:49:10.800
It was great.
太棒了。

1196
00:49:11.060 --> 00:49:12.580
I have another fan question.
我还有另一个粉丝问题。

1197
00:49:12.720 --> 00:49:15.460
Donna asked, was anyone hurt by the fireworks?
唐娜问，有人被烟花炸伤吗？

1198
00:49:15.660 --> 00:49:16.780
That looked kind of dangerous.
看起来挺危险的。

1199
00:49:17.440 --> 00:49:21.920
So I saw Brian Baumgartner recently, and I asked him about the fireworks.
我最近见到了布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳，我问了他关于烟花的事。

1200
00:49:22.240 --> 00:49:25.040
He said, Jenna, it was insane.
他说，珍娜，那简直太疯狂了。

1201
00:49:26.160 --> 00:49:30.220
There was no stunt coordinator for these fireworks.
拍这些烟花戏时没有特技指导。

1202
00:49:30.520 --> 00:49:37.580
He said, because they had to get the shot of us from so far away, they really left the
他说，因为必须从很远的地方拍我们，所以他们真的把

1203
00:49:37.580 --> 00:49:41.760
two of them out in the middle of this parking lot field alone.
我们俩单独留在了停车场那片空地上。

1204
00:49:41.760 --> 00:49:43.920
Which looked very dry.
看起来非常干燥。

1205
00:49:44.300 --> 00:49:44.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1206
00:49:44.740 --> 00:49:47.260
Well, you know, fireworks are illegal in L.A.
嗯，你知道，在洛杉矶放烟花是违法的。

1207
00:49:47.480 --> 00:49:48.040
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1208
00:49:48.040 --> 00:49:51.000
They had a hard time even getting fireworks for this scene.
他们甚至很难为这场戏弄到烟花。

1209
00:49:51.020 --> 00:49:52.220
We were breaking the law?
我们当时在违法吗？

1210
00:49:52.380 --> 00:49:53.360
I'm not sure.
我不确定。

1211
00:49:53.740 --> 00:50:01.640
I know BJ said once in an article that there was a rule about how big the fireworks could be.
我知道BJ曾经在一篇文章里说过，关于烟花的大小是有规定的。

1212
00:50:01.640 --> 00:50:05.020
They weren't allowed to shoot anything up in the air because L.A.
他们不被允许向空中发射任何东西，因为洛杉矶

1213
00:50:05.100 --> 00:50:05.780
is very dry.
非常干燥。

1214
00:50:06.020 --> 00:50:06.560
That's right.
没错。

1215
00:50:06.660 --> 00:50:07.680
I think I do know that.
我想我确实知道这一点。

1216
00:50:07.840 --> 00:50:09.440
So you can do the thing that's on the ground.
所以你只能玩那种在地面上的。

1217
00:50:09.520 --> 00:50:10.580
But that's it.
但也就仅此而已了。

1218
00:50:10.700 --> 00:50:10.900
Yes.
是的。

1219
00:50:11.020 --> 00:50:13.140
So they were like the sparkler thing on the ground.
所以他们就像是在地上玩那种手持烟花。

1220
00:50:13.200 --> 00:50:13.600
Yes.
是的。

1221
00:50:15.160 --> 00:50:19.360
And Brian said that they couldn't hear anything.
布莱恩说他们什么也听不见。

1222
00:50:19.460 --> 00:50:21.580
They could barely hear action or cut.
他们几乎听不到“开始”或“停”的指令。

1223
00:50:21.880 --> 00:50:24.220
They just were out there playing in these fireworks.
他们只是在那儿玩烟花。

1224
00:50:24.220 --> 00:50:32.860
But at a certain point, he heard someone shout, hop over them, kick them, like stuff like that.
但在某个时刻，他听到有人大喊，跳过去，踢开它们，诸如此类的话。

1225
00:50:33.000 --> 00:50:33.100
It was probably Greg.
那可能是格雷格。

1226
00:50:33.100 --> 00:50:34.680
It was probably Greg screaming.
那可能是格雷格在尖叫。

1227
00:50:35.640 --> 00:50:38.840
But Brian said they were just – it felt very real.
但布莱恩说他们当时只是——感觉非常真实。

1228
00:50:38.900 --> 00:50:48.140
And I think that was part of it about what made that night so magical was that it was really like we were watching those guys goof around with fireworks.
我认为这也是那一晚如此神奇的原因之一，因为我们真的就像是在看那两个家伙玩烟花。

1229
00:50:48.260 --> 00:50:49.020
Because they were.
因为他们确实在玩。

1230
00:50:49.160 --> 00:50:50.020
Because you were.
因为你们确实在玩。

1231
00:50:50.760 --> 00:50:51.320
Yes.
是的。

1232
00:50:51.620 --> 00:50:52.180
Yes.
是的。

1233
00:50:52.180 --> 00:51:00.180
And after this, when we come down from the roof, you know, Jim and Pam, they leave the office and they're listening on the headphones.
在这之后，当我们从屋顶下来时，你知道，吉姆和帕姆离开了办公室，他们戴着耳机在听。

1234
00:51:00.520 --> 00:51:06.440
Oh, at 14 minutes, 34 seconds, I have a note card that says, old tech alert.
哦，在14分34秒的时候，我有一张笔记卡写着：老式科技警报。

1235
00:51:07.020 --> 00:51:07.460
What?
什么？

1236
00:51:07.840 --> 00:51:09.520
Because it's an iPod.
因为那是iPod。

1237
00:51:09.700 --> 00:51:10.140
Yes.
是的。

1238
00:51:10.260 --> 00:51:11.500
It's an iPod.
那是iPod。

1239
00:51:11.500 --> 00:51:14.580
And you guys have like the little headphones where you each take a little ear.
你们戴着那种小耳机，每人分戴一只。

1240
00:51:14.780 --> 00:51:15.580
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

1241
00:51:15.580 --> 00:51:22.700
Well, Matt Hurt asked, what, if anything, were you and John listening to when you shot the swaying dancing scene?
嗯，马特·赫特问，在拍摄摇摆舞那场戏时，你和约翰听的是什么歌（如果有的话）？

1242
00:51:22.880 --> 00:51:23.240
Okay.
好的。

1243
00:51:23.320 --> 00:51:25.000
That's one of my questions too, Matt.
这也是我的问题之一，马特。

1244
00:51:25.160 --> 00:51:26.160
So what was it?
所以那是什么歌？

1245
00:51:26.320 --> 00:51:26.700
Okay.
好的。

1246
00:51:26.940 --> 00:51:31.620
The song you hear in the episode is a song called Sing by Travis.
你们在剧集中听到的那首歌是特拉维斯乐队的《Sing》。

1247
00:51:32.200 --> 00:51:36.400
But John and I were actually listening to an Interpol song.
但我和约翰当时实际上听的是Interpol乐队的一首歌。

1248
00:51:37.000 --> 00:51:37.780
Which song?
哪首歌？

1249
00:51:37.820 --> 00:51:38.600
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

1250
00:51:38.600 --> 00:51:40.020
But you know it was Interpol.
但你知道那是Interpol的歌。

1251
00:51:40.180 --> 00:51:40.460
Yes.
是的。

1252
00:51:40.640 --> 00:51:41.600
I remember that.
我记得那个。

1253
00:51:41.740 --> 00:51:50.440
And I think, I think that was John's actual iPod and that he suggested that song, that we listened to the song.
