00:58:03.160 --> 00:58:05.540
that she did something she shouldn't have, I think.
我是这么认为的。

1408
00:58:05.540 --> 00:58:10.800
Well, I think whenever like there's a moment when Angela catches her with Pam Pong, then
嗯，我觉得每当安吉拉撞见她和帕姆打乒乓球的时候，或者

1409
00:58:10.800 --> 00:58:13.120
Meredith catches the shirt coming up, right?
梅雷迪思看到她撩起衬衫的时候，对吧？

1410
00:58:13.360 --> 00:58:18.040
And then this moment when he calls it out, all of those moments are when Pam gets a mirror
还有当他指出这一点的时候，所有这些时刻都是帕姆在面对自己行为的镜子，

1411
00:58:18.040 --> 00:58:24.240
held up to her behavior, and it makes her uncomfortable because she knows the right thing to do is say,
这让她感到不安，因为她知道正确的做法应该是说，

1412
00:58:24.360 --> 00:58:27.300
Roy, I'm in love with Jim, and we should break up.
罗伊，我爱上了吉姆，我们应该分手。

1413
00:58:27.480 --> 00:58:27.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1414
00:58:27.620 --> 00:58:32.060
But she's got all of these layers like you do in a relationship, and feelings probably of guilt
但她身上背负着各种包袱，就像你在一段关系中会有的那样，可能还有内疚感

1415
00:58:32.060 --> 00:58:35.260
and obligation, and all of that all wrapped up into it.
和责任感，所有这些都交织在一起。

1416
00:58:35.320 --> 00:58:37.040
So she doesn't know how to make that break.
所以她不知道该如何做出那个了断。

1417
00:58:37.240 --> 00:58:37.500
Yeah.
没错。

1418
00:58:37.660 --> 00:58:41.840
And I think this is one of those moments where a mirror is held up, and she feels bad,
我觉得这就是那种让她照镜子的时刻，她感到难受，

1419
00:58:41.920 --> 00:58:42.900
and she bristles at it.
并因此感到不适。

1420
00:58:42.980 --> 00:58:48.080
And then it all ends with that final look between Michael and Jim, the little shrug.
最后以迈克尔和吉姆之间那个眼神交流结束，就是那个小小的耸肩。

1421
00:58:48.800 --> 00:58:49.680
Eh, women.
唉，女人啊。

1422
00:58:49.960 --> 00:58:51.240
Ah, what are you going to do?
啊，你能怎么办呢？

1423
00:58:51.380 --> 00:58:51.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1424
00:58:52.920 --> 00:58:54.000
Two lonely guys.
两个孤独的男人。

1425
00:58:54.480 --> 00:58:56.200
Well, guys, that was the client.
好了，伙计们，那是客户。

1426
00:58:56.200 --> 00:58:57.400
That's the client.
那是客户。

1427
00:58:57.600 --> 00:59:02.260
Thank you so much, Melora Hardin and Tim Meadows for making this episode that much more special.
非常感谢梅洛拉·哈丁和蒂姆·梅多斯让这一集变得如此特别。

1428
00:59:02.480 --> 00:59:06.860
And I want to say thank you to Brian Baumgartner and Phil Shea and Greg Daniels,
我也想感谢布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳、菲尔·谢伊和格雷格·丹尼尔斯，

1429
00:59:06.980 --> 00:59:09.040
all of whom I reached out to for this episode.
这一集我向他们所有人都寻求了帮助。

1430
00:59:09.200 --> 00:59:10.120
Thanks, guys, for your help.
谢谢你们的帮助，伙计们。

1431
00:59:10.340 --> 00:59:11.180
Thanks, everybody.
谢谢大家。

1432
00:59:11.480 --> 00:59:12.840
All right, we'll see you next week.
好了，我们下周见。

1433
00:59:12.980 --> 00:59:15.900
We're going to be chunking performance review your way.
下周我们将为大家带来“绩效评估”那一集。

1434
00:59:16.660 --> 00:59:17.460
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1435
00:59:18.480 --> 00:59:19.280
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1436
00:59:19.580 --> 00:59:21.560
Hey, I'm proud of us for pulling it back together.
嘿，我为我们能重新找回状态感到自豪。

1437
00:59:21.660 --> 00:59:23.620
We were really on the edge at the beginning of this one.
这一集刚开始的时候我们真的有点失控了。

1438
00:59:23.620 --> 00:59:24.660
I got a little giddy.
我当时有点头晕。

1439
00:59:24.660 --> 00:59:27.380
I was a little punchy, so thanks for sticking it out.
我有点语无伦次，所以谢谢你们坚持听完。

1440
00:59:27.600 --> 00:59:28.880
That's what she said.
那是她说的。

1441
00:59:29.160 --> 00:59:29.940
Ooh, good ending.
噢，不错的结尾。

1442
00:59:30.120 --> 00:59:30.440
Thank you.
谢谢。

1443
00:59:32.060 --> 00:59:34.040
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

